1
00:00:03,313 --> 00:00:04,823
Why are you pouring drinks yourself?

2
00:00:09,953 --> 00:00:11,893
You shouldn't drink on an empty stomach, Dad.

3
00:00:15,893 --> 00:00:17,293
What's wrong?

4
00:00:20,203 --> 00:00:22,333
Why are you just drinking instead of eating?

5
00:00:32,013 --> 00:00:33,013
Seung Ri.

6
00:00:34,113 --> 00:00:35,783
Listen carefully to what I'm about to say.

7
00:00:39,123 --> 00:00:40,153
I...

8
00:00:43,493 --> 00:00:44,593
have a criminal record.

9
00:00:48,233 --> 00:00:49,233
Dad.

10
00:00:51,803 --> 00:00:52,803
I'm sorry.

11
00:00:54,303 --> 00:00:55,873
I'm sorry that I have to be the one to tell you this.

12
00:00:57,833 --> 00:00:59,703
Twenty-five years ago,

13
00:01:00,673 --> 00:01:02,113
I caused a car accident.

14
00:01:04,613 --> 00:01:06,443
Someone died in that accident...

15
00:01:09,013 --> 00:01:10,113
I know, Dad.

16
00:01:11,153 --> 00:01:15,223
But, I always suspected...

17
00:01:16,293 --> 00:01:17,453
that it was unavoidable.

18
00:01:19,923 --> 00:01:20,923
That's right.

19
00:01:22,333 --> 00:01:23,593
It was out of my control.

20
00:01:34,843 --> 00:01:35,843
Because of that incident...

21
00:01:37,213 --> 00:01:39,443
I was in prison for five years.

22
00:01:40,813 --> 00:01:42,553
I wasn't transferred to the Europe office.

23
00:01:44,923 --> 00:01:46,123
Jung Dong Pal...

24
00:01:47,023 --> 00:01:48,293
He was my cellmate.

25
00:01:48,653 --> 00:01:49,653
Stop.

26
00:01:51,353 --> 00:01:52,393
That's enough.

27
00:01:53,593 --> 00:01:57,133
- But, you already served your time. - Yes.

28
00:01:57,763 --> 00:01:59,163
I used to think so.

29
00:02:00,133 --> 00:02:01,573
That I had paid for my crime.

30
00:02:03,073 --> 00:02:04,133
But...

31
00:02:05,703 --> 00:02:06,703
I was wrong.

32
00:02:09,143 --> 00:02:13,043
How could I ever truly pay for it when someone died?

33
00:02:15,013 --> 00:02:16,583
And in the end, because of my sin,

34
00:02:17,353 --> 00:02:19,323
you were the one who had to go through something so terrible.

35
00:02:21,923 --> 00:02:24,623
- How did you find out? - Why on earth would you do that?

36
00:02:25,323 --> 00:02:26,323
Why?

37
00:02:27,423 --> 00:02:28,933
I'm the one who committed the crime.

38
00:02:31,093 --> 00:02:33,703
Why did you have to suffer because of me?

39
00:02:33,903 --> 00:02:36,333
I happened to overhear him blackmailing you.

40
00:02:38,203 --> 00:02:40,843
Seeing you getting tormented by his blackmail,

41
00:02:40,903 --> 00:02:42,873
I just couldn't stand by and do nothing.

42
00:02:43,843 --> 00:02:45,183
That's why I stepped in.

43
00:02:45,383 --> 00:02:48,883
You're just lucky that's all that happened.

44
00:02:49,913 --> 00:02:51,453
If you had gotten seriously hurt...

45
00:02:53,023 --> 00:02:54,023
That man,

46
00:02:54,323 --> 00:02:57,193
he's not the kind of person you can handle.

47
00:02:59,623 --> 00:03:01,693
What were you thinking, doing something so reckless?

48
00:03:03,633 --> 00:03:04,863
I'm sorry, Dad.

49
00:03:06,803 --> 00:03:10,373
I'll never make you worry like that again.

50
00:03:13,073 --> 00:03:14,573
I may not have been a good father...

51
00:03:16,173 --> 00:03:17,613
to you and Seung Woo,

52
00:03:18,213 --> 00:03:21,243
or a respectable husband to your mother,

53
00:03:21,983 --> 00:03:25,683
My family is my everything to me.

54
00:03:27,453 --> 00:03:29,693
If you had gotten hurt in any way because of me,

55
00:03:30,593 --> 00:03:31,893
I wouldn't be able to live.

56
00:03:33,493 --> 00:03:36,193
Who do you think I have been working for all this time?

57
00:03:36,863 --> 00:03:38,533
Why do you think I have come this far?

58
00:03:39,503 --> 00:03:40,563
Please...

59
00:03:41,463 --> 00:03:43,633
cherish yourself and take care, Seung Ri.

60
00:03:47,243 --> 00:03:48,543
I will, Dad.

61
00:03:50,573 --> 00:03:51,573
I promise.

62
00:03:52,143 --> 00:03:53,213
From now on,

63
00:03:54,143 --> 00:03:56,713
I'll truly cherish myself and take care.

64
00:04:01,993 --> 00:04:02,993
I'm sorry.

65
00:04:11,193 --> 00:04:12,633
Let's go around one more time.

66
00:04:12,763 --> 00:04:14,973
What? But, we've already gone around three times.

67
00:04:15,533 --> 00:04:17,633
I feel bad for being the only one to get a gift.

68
00:04:17,703 --> 00:04:20,503
If I had known, I would've prepared a gift too.

69
00:04:20,743 --> 00:04:21,973
Hey, what are you talking about?

70
00:04:22,043 --> 00:04:23,813
You're the one who gave me a dreamcatcher...

71
00:04:23,873 --> 00:04:24,873
for my room yesterday.

72
00:04:25,283 --> 00:04:26,983
I think I'll be able to sleep soundly...

73
00:04:27,043 --> 00:04:29,553
without nightmares from now on. Thanks to you, Eun Ae.

74
00:04:29,853 --> 00:04:31,183
I really hope so.

75
00:04:33,523 --> 00:04:34,653
It's so pretty.

76
00:04:37,693 --> 00:04:38,693
What?

77
00:04:38,993 --> 00:04:41,063
Why are you taking that off? It's your trademark.

78
00:04:41,263 --> 00:04:44,193
- You've never taken it off before. - I know. It's my trademark.

79
00:04:44,793 --> 00:04:46,863
- Give me your hand. - My hand?

80
00:04:47,333 --> 00:04:48,333
Okay.

81
00:04:50,203 --> 00:04:52,643
There. My trademark...

82
00:04:52,943 --> 00:04:54,403
is now yours, Team Leader Ko.

83
00:04:57,743 --> 00:04:59,813
This reminds me of the day we first met.

84
00:05:03,013 --> 00:05:05,653
No cash in the wallet, and I'll cancel the cards,

85
00:05:05,653 --> 00:05:06,653
so they're useless.

86
00:05:06,853 --> 00:05:07,853
While the wallet is a designer brand,

87
00:05:07,923 --> 00:05:10,553
I've had it for over ten years, so it's not worth much.

88
00:05:10,853 --> 00:05:12,223
So just hand it over quietly.

89
00:05:13,023 --> 00:05:15,333
Are you insane? Let go of me!

90
00:05:16,163 --> 00:05:17,163
Hey, hold on...

91
00:05:27,003 --> 00:05:30,143
Back then, that we would end up together like this...

92
00:05:30,613 --> 00:05:32,143
I could not have imagined it at all.

93
00:05:33,013 --> 00:05:34,013
Tell me about it.

94
00:05:34,683 --> 00:05:36,513
It is funny how people end up together.

95
00:05:38,013 --> 00:05:39,883
For some reason, I feel that wearing this...

96
00:05:39,953 --> 00:05:41,383
will always bring me good luck,

97
00:05:41,583 --> 00:05:43,093
and that only good things will happen.

98
00:05:43,593 --> 00:05:45,693
Just like its name, Lucky Joy.

99
00:05:46,223 --> 00:05:47,693
Of course. It has to.

100
00:05:48,363 --> 00:05:50,263
- You should head in now. - Okay.

101
00:05:56,503 --> 00:05:58,943
Knitting? In the middle of this heat wave?

102
00:06:00,143 --> 00:06:03,873
- I have to start now for winter. - What are you knitting?

103
00:06:04,773 --> 00:06:05,843
You will see.

104
00:06:06,383 --> 00:06:07,983
Did Eun Ae and Team Leader Ko get back?

105
00:06:08,413 --> 00:06:09,483
Yes, a little while ago.

106
00:06:11,183 --> 00:06:13,753
Honey, have you given it some thought?

107
00:06:14,453 --> 00:06:15,453
About what?

108
00:06:16,093 --> 00:06:21,833
The Chairman wants to make you his daughter officially, on paper.

109
00:06:22,833 --> 00:06:24,893
And it seems President Ko is getting very tense about it.

110
00:06:25,663 --> 00:06:27,533
He asked me today what you are going to do.

111
00:06:29,873 --> 00:06:31,433
Honestly, my feeling is that...

112
00:06:32,173 --> 00:06:34,103
finding my mother is enough.

113
00:06:34,173 --> 00:06:36,843
What is the point of a legal document?

114
00:06:37,913 --> 00:06:39,583
But, after hearing what the Chairman said,

115
00:06:40,513 --> 00:06:43,553
I am also conflicted.

116
00:06:44,683 --> 00:06:46,353
When I think of my childhood,

117
00:06:47,053 --> 00:06:48,383
not even knowing my real name or age,

118
00:06:48,653 --> 00:06:51,353
moving from house to house, orphanage to orphanage,

119
00:06:51,453 --> 00:06:53,763
when I think of my childhood moving around...

120
00:06:54,593 --> 00:06:56,563
even now, as my mother's daughter,

121
00:06:56,563 --> 00:06:57,593
I cannot deny that a part of me wants...

122
00:06:57,663 --> 00:06:59,063
to make things official on paper.

123
00:07:00,563 --> 00:07:02,533
But, when I think of President Ko and his wife,

124
00:07:02,603 --> 00:07:04,433
trembling with fear that it might happen...

125
00:07:07,073 --> 00:07:08,813
I know exactly how you feel.

126
00:07:09,813 --> 00:07:12,383
There is no rush, so think it over carefully...

127
00:07:13,243 --> 00:07:14,943
and do whatever you want most.

128
00:07:17,583 --> 00:07:19,653
Wait a minute. What time is it?

129
00:07:20,653 --> 00:07:24,093
- It is 10:55. Why? - That girl. I swear.

130
00:07:26,123 --> 00:07:27,293
(Our Happy Days Real Estate, Grandma Pancake)

131
00:07:27,393 --> 00:07:30,533
Wait a minute. Hey, wait, Eun Nim.

132
00:07:31,963 --> 00:07:32,963
Seung Woo.

133
00:07:33,933 --> 00:07:34,933
What was that all about?

134
00:07:35,273 --> 00:07:37,673
I have been calling your name since the bus stop.

135
00:07:37,773 --> 00:07:39,543
I did not hear you.

136
00:07:40,043 --> 00:07:41,073
But, why are you here?

137
00:07:41,403 --> 00:07:42,743
Are you Cinderella or something?

138
00:07:42,813 --> 00:07:44,943
At the stroke of midnight, no, that is not it.

139
00:07:45,073 --> 00:07:46,383
It is not like the clock is striking 11, either.

140
00:07:46,813 --> 00:07:51,153
- Why did you rush out mid-writing? - Cinderella?

141
00:07:51,653 --> 00:07:53,023
What are you talking about?

142
00:07:53,783 --> 00:07:56,493
And besides, I am wearing my shoes perfectly fine.

143
00:07:57,493 --> 00:07:58,663
That is not it.

144
00:07:59,823 --> 00:08:00,823
Your bag.

145
00:08:01,293 --> 00:08:05,403
- That is my bag. - Oh no. Sorry, Bung Woo.

146
00:08:08,003 --> 00:08:09,403
Here you go.

147
00:08:15,813 --> 00:08:16,813
Jo Eun Nim.

148
00:08:17,413 --> 00:08:18,683
Mom.

149
00:08:19,383 --> 00:08:20,483
Do you know what time it is?

150
00:08:20,543 --> 00:08:22,213
Did I tell you to be home by eleven or not?

151
00:08:22,453 --> 00:08:24,213
Good evening, ma'am.

152
00:08:24,783 --> 00:08:25,783
Ma'am?

153
00:08:28,283 --> 00:08:31,253
Well, I should be going then. Have a pleasant night.

154
00:08:32,193 --> 00:08:33,193
Bung Nim.

155
00:08:34,823 --> 00:08:37,333
- Good night. - Bye, Bung Woo.

156
00:08:38,293 --> 00:08:40,833
Bung Woo? Bung Nim? Honestly, you two.

157
00:08:40,903 --> 00:08:43,603
Get inside. Go on, hurry up and get inside. Goodness.

158
00:08:43,673 --> 00:08:44,673
Get going.

159
00:08:50,743 --> 00:08:53,313
Tell me. Seriously, my Bung Woo...

160
00:08:54,083 --> 00:08:55,753
I mean, why do you hate Seung Woo so much?

161
00:08:55,853 --> 00:08:57,613
You've been going on about "Bung Woo" and "Bung Nim."

162
00:08:57,683 --> 00:08:59,053
Are those your pet names for each other?

163
00:08:59,123 --> 00:09:03,093
- Are you two really dating? - Not exactly...

164
00:09:03,353 --> 00:09:05,123
No, but seriously, why do you hate him so much?

165
00:09:05,463 --> 00:09:07,523
I don't like the way he looks. That's why.

166
00:09:07,593 --> 00:09:09,933
What? What's wrong with his looks? He's so handsome.

167
00:09:10,093 --> 00:09:11,793
Haven't you heard that pretty boys are trouble?

168
00:09:12,133 --> 00:09:13,833
He's probably swarming with girls, right?

169
00:09:13,963 --> 00:09:17,333
No, not swarming. Maybe just one?

170
00:09:17,503 --> 00:09:20,443
Either way, he's obviously the type that attracts girls.

171
00:09:20,503 --> 00:09:21,503
Is it a crime to be handsome?

172
00:09:21,573 --> 00:09:23,213
If that's the case, what about Team Leader Ko?

173
00:09:23,373 --> 00:09:24,373
Team Leader Ko is handsome, too.

174
00:09:24,443 --> 00:09:25,583
Why aren't you trying to stop Seung Ri?

175
00:09:25,643 --> 00:09:27,943
Are you saying their good looks are the same?

176
00:09:28,213 --> 00:09:30,713
Anyone can see Team Leader Ko has strong principles,

177
00:09:30,783 --> 00:09:32,553
no matter who tries to sway him,

178
00:09:32,623 --> 00:09:34,083
he looks like he'd stand his ground.

179
00:09:34,153 --> 00:09:36,223
That kid from before, if someone tried to sway him,

180
00:09:36,293 --> 00:09:39,223
he seems like he'd be easily swayed and unreliable.

181
00:09:39,293 --> 00:09:43,233
Wow, Mom, that's ridiculous. Do you even know Bung Woo?

182
00:09:43,433 --> 00:09:46,303
- Do you? - That's not all.

183
00:09:46,303 --> 00:09:48,033
I don't like his job either.

184
00:09:48,103 --> 00:09:51,903
No matter what, a man needs to have a stable job.

185
00:09:52,503 --> 00:09:53,543
What's a webtoon artist?

186
00:09:53,603 --> 00:09:55,773
How is he supposed to make a living drawing comics?

187
00:09:55,843 --> 00:09:56,913
This isn't going to end.

188
00:09:57,413 --> 00:10:00,183
By that logic, your daughter is a web novel writer.

189
00:10:00,443 --> 00:10:02,253
Mom, it's impossible to even have a conversation with you.

190
00:10:02,683 --> 00:10:03,683
What do you mean?

191
00:10:03,753 --> 00:10:05,153
Do you think I'm doing this for myself?

192
00:10:05,213 --> 00:10:07,383
You're going to say, "This is all for your own good,"

193
00:10:07,453 --> 00:10:08,453
aren't you, Mom?

194
00:10:09,423 --> 00:10:10,423
Unbelievable.

195
00:10:13,523 --> 00:10:14,763
Are you feeling a bit better, Dad?

196
00:10:17,193 --> 00:10:18,803
I'm fine now.

197
00:10:20,763 --> 00:10:23,503
Seung Ri, let me ask you for one more favour.

198
00:10:25,133 --> 00:10:26,943
Yes, tell me.

199
00:10:29,073 --> 00:10:30,743
The things we talked about today,

200
00:10:31,713 --> 00:10:32,743
let's take them to our graves.

201
00:10:37,053 --> 00:10:39,283
Seung Woo and your mother must never find out.

202
00:10:40,823 --> 00:10:41,823
Got it?

203
00:10:42,623 --> 00:10:45,493
Of course. I know exactly what you mean.

204
00:10:49,233 --> 00:10:50,893
Gosh.

205
00:10:51,993 --> 00:10:54,203
Why on earth does she dislike me so much?

206
00:10:54,603 --> 00:10:55,733
Bung Nim's mother.

207
00:10:57,373 --> 00:10:59,873
I want to make a good impression.

208
00:11:04,343 --> 00:11:05,343
What?

209
00:11:06,483 --> 00:11:07,483
Dad.

210
00:11:07,743 --> 00:11:09,953
- Seung Ri. - Hey, Seung Woo.

211
00:11:10,513 --> 00:11:11,583
What are you two doing here?

212
00:11:12,253 --> 00:11:14,153
Gosh, what secrets are you two whispering about?

213
00:11:14,383 --> 00:11:15,723
What secrets?

214
00:11:15,993 --> 00:11:18,923
- I had a date with Dad. Why? - A date?

215
00:11:19,793 --> 00:11:20,793
Hold on.

216
00:11:21,923 --> 00:11:23,733
Is that the smell of ribs?

217
00:11:24,433 --> 00:11:26,733
Don't tell me you two just went out for ribs?

218
00:11:27,363 --> 00:11:28,933
Seung Woo, I'm sorry.

219
00:11:29,503 --> 00:11:31,173
I had to discuss something about work...

220
00:11:31,233 --> 00:11:34,903
with your sister today. Next time, let's all go as a family.

221
00:11:34,973 --> 00:11:38,343
Wait a minute. Does that mean Mom's been home alone all this time?

222
00:11:38,573 --> 00:11:39,583
What?

223
00:11:40,243 --> 00:11:42,353
Mom's menopause symptoms have seemed really bad lately.

224
00:11:42,813 --> 00:11:45,553
- We're in big trouble. - Kids, let's go.

225
00:11:45,823 --> 00:11:47,753
- Okay. - Oh, honestly.

226
00:11:48,353 --> 00:11:49,923
- Hurry. - Run.

227
00:11:52,093 --> 00:11:54,563
Mom, we're home.

228
00:11:55,763 --> 00:11:57,163
Mom, are you sleeping?

229
00:11:58,233 --> 00:11:59,263
We're here.

230
00:12:02,703 --> 00:12:05,233
What do we do? I think she's really upset with us.

231
00:12:07,743 --> 00:12:08,743
Honey.

232
00:12:09,873 --> 00:12:12,413
Seung Ri and I were delayed talking about work,

233
00:12:13,013 --> 00:12:15,583
and we ran into Seung Woo right outside.

234
00:12:16,083 --> 00:12:19,053
I'm sorry. Next time, we'll be sure to go together...

235
00:12:21,523 --> 00:12:22,893
Oh, come on, Mom.

236
00:12:30,963 --> 00:12:33,563
(Gangsu Construction)

237
00:12:35,133 --> 00:12:36,303
Are you almost done?

238
00:12:36,573 --> 00:12:38,733
Everyone else went to lunch. Should we go too?

239
00:12:39,573 --> 00:12:41,673
What? Oh, were you waiting for me?

240
00:12:42,143 --> 00:12:44,843
You should go get some lunch. I have to go somewhere.

241
00:12:45,113 --> 00:12:46,113
Where to?

242
00:12:47,643 --> 00:12:48,683
The police station.

243
00:12:48,983 --> 00:12:50,313
The police station? Why?

244
00:12:50,983 --> 00:12:52,583
I'm going to look up some of my father's records.

245
00:12:53,123 --> 00:12:54,883
It's been a long time, so I'm not sure...

246
00:12:54,953 --> 00:12:57,553
- if I'll find anything. - In that case, I'll go with you.

247
00:12:57,623 --> 00:12:59,393
I don't feel right about you going alone.

248
00:12:59,623 --> 00:13:02,093
No, it's okay. This might take a while,

249
00:13:02,163 --> 00:13:04,233
so I took a half-day off. You should get back to work, Eun Ae.

250
00:13:04,293 --> 00:13:05,803
Are you sure you'll be okay on your own?

251
00:13:06,103 --> 00:13:10,473
Of course. I've got this with me. I'll just pretend you're with me.

252
00:13:12,373 --> 00:13:13,503
Well, shall I get going?

253
00:13:15,513 --> 00:13:18,013
(Police)

254
00:13:18,073 --> 00:13:19,283
(To Improve The Public's Perception Of Safety)

255
00:13:19,343 --> 00:13:21,043
(Mobile Civil Complaint Counselling)

256
00:13:22,753 --> 00:13:24,513
(Application For Traffic Accident Report)

257
00:13:24,583 --> 00:13:25,983
(Applicant: Ko Gyeol)

258
00:13:26,053 --> 00:13:27,383
(Date Of Accident: May 16, 2001)

259
00:13:27,453 --> 00:13:28,683
(Location)

260
00:13:32,963 --> 00:13:35,363
(Location)

261
00:13:35,893 --> 00:13:36,893
Excuse me.

262
00:13:37,263 --> 00:13:39,403
I don't know where the accident occurred.

263
00:13:39,463 --> 00:13:40,903
Can I still get the report?

264
00:13:41,433 --> 00:13:43,433
- Let me check for you. - Okay.

265
00:13:46,303 --> 00:13:48,913
An accident in 2001? So, 25 years ago?

266
00:13:49,113 --> 00:13:50,213
Yes, that's right.

267
00:13:51,573 --> 00:13:53,643
This probably wouldn't have been digitized.

268
00:14:01,483 --> 00:14:03,853
I'm sorry, but we can't find it on our end.

269
00:14:04,523 --> 00:14:06,923
Does that mean there's no way to find it at all?

270
00:14:07,063 --> 00:14:08,293
Not necessarily.

271
00:14:08,563 --> 00:14:10,393
You should try going to the station that had jurisdiction.

272
00:14:10,793 --> 00:14:11,893
The station with jurisdiction?

273
00:14:11,993 --> 00:14:14,303
Yes, the one that handled the accident at the time.

274
00:14:14,763 --> 00:14:16,633
The files might still be there.

275
00:14:16,933 --> 00:14:18,633
If it's the station that handled the accident,

276
00:14:19,003 --> 00:14:20,673
I need to know where it happened, right?

277
00:14:20,673 --> 00:14:21,773
Right.

278
00:14:21,843 --> 00:14:24,243
(Officer Kim Jun Ho)

279
00:14:24,313 --> 00:14:26,083
You don't remember the location at all?

280
00:14:27,213 --> 00:14:28,213
No.

281
00:14:29,913 --> 00:14:31,513
Then I'll try to run a case search...

282
00:14:31,583 --> 00:14:33,353
with the information you've provided.

283
00:14:34,083 --> 00:14:35,453
Yes, thank you.

284
00:14:43,993 --> 00:14:48,403
- Okay, look at me, all right? - Okay.

285
00:14:48,733 --> 00:14:49,833
One, two.

286
00:14:50,973 --> 00:14:52,273
One, two, three.

287
00:14:52,903 --> 00:14:55,473
- One, two, three. - Ma'am,

288
00:14:55,473 --> 00:14:57,513
- your sense of rhythm is... - One, two, three, four, one, two.

289
00:14:57,673 --> 00:15:00,383
a natural gift. If you had gone into showbiz...

290
00:15:00,443 --> 00:15:02,313
instead of making pancakes,

291
00:15:02,313 --> 00:15:05,483
you could've easily become a famous pop singer.

292
00:15:05,553 --> 00:15:10,053
Right? If I had gone that route back in the day,

293
00:15:10,523 --> 00:15:14,223
Kim Chu Ja, Jeong Hun Hui, and Hye Eun Yi,

294
00:15:14,293 --> 00:15:17,393
- they would've starved. - Right.

295
00:15:18,133 --> 00:15:19,163
My goodness.

296
00:15:21,433 --> 00:15:22,873
- Have you been waiting long? - Oh, my.

297
00:15:23,303 --> 00:15:26,603
We could have just come on our own. Why did you send a car?

298
00:15:26,873 --> 00:15:28,603
We've troubled you so much, Mr. Ju.

299
00:15:28,843 --> 00:15:33,243
Oh, it's no trouble at all. The Chairman is so excited...

300
00:15:33,313 --> 00:15:35,653
at the thought of seeing his grandchildren...

301
00:15:35,713 --> 00:15:37,053
and great-granddaughter.

302
00:15:38,113 --> 00:15:39,753
- Shall we get going? - Yes.

303
00:15:39,753 --> 00:15:42,023
- Ms. Park, see you at the studio. - Okay. Take care.

304
00:15:42,793 --> 00:15:47,223
My, they say life is full of twists and turns.

305
00:15:47,523 --> 00:15:49,663
Who would have thought Eun Hyung's family...

306
00:15:49,733 --> 00:15:51,493
would have such a joyous occasion?

307
00:15:51,593 --> 00:15:55,003
- Hardly an occasion. I'll be back. - Okay.

308
00:15:57,533 --> 00:15:58,633
Let's go.

309
00:15:58,633 --> 00:15:59,843
- Yes, let's go. - Bit Na looks so pretty.

310
00:16:00,743 --> 00:16:03,173
Bit Na, have a good time at your great-grandmother's house.

311
00:16:03,273 --> 00:16:06,183
- Okay, Auntie. Bye-bye. - Let's go.

312
00:16:06,243 --> 00:16:07,583
- Bye-bye. - Bit Na, let's go.

313
00:16:09,553 --> 00:16:12,353
Eun Hyung looks amazing in that suit.

314
00:16:12,653 --> 00:16:15,853
- Right, Grandma? - Amazing in what? Speak clearly.

315
00:16:16,293 --> 00:16:18,693
You know, when I was little, I used to have this fantasy.

316
00:16:18,753 --> 00:16:20,623
- Yes? - That I was secretly...

317
00:16:20,693 --> 00:16:22,263
the long-lost daughter of a rich family,

318
00:16:22,323 --> 00:16:24,163
and my birth mother would come looking for me.

319
00:16:24,233 --> 00:16:25,333
Then what about me? What am I,

320
00:16:25,393 --> 00:16:27,063
the one who worked her butt off to raise you?

321
00:16:28,003 --> 00:16:29,973
I'm just saying it was a fantasy I used to have.

322
00:16:30,873 --> 00:16:32,443
- Anyway, Grandma. - Yes?

323
00:16:32,503 --> 00:16:34,573
What's the deal with you and Yong Man, or Secretary Ju?

324
00:16:34,873 --> 00:16:35,913
The deal?

325
00:16:35,973 --> 00:16:39,883
What in the world are you talking about?

326
00:16:40,243 --> 00:16:43,253
He's a younger friend who drops by my restaurant.

327
00:16:43,553 --> 00:16:45,683
We're in the same line dancing class.

328
00:16:46,423 --> 00:16:48,883
- Why? - I mean... Right.

329
00:16:49,623 --> 00:16:51,623
Yes, I guess my imagination got carried away.

330
00:16:51,693 --> 00:16:55,523
- What were you imagining now? - It's nothing.

331
00:16:57,063 --> 00:17:01,863
Gosh. You are so bland, you must not eat enough salt.

332
00:17:03,703 --> 00:17:06,403
It's a shame Eun Ae isn't here with us,

333
00:17:07,003 --> 00:17:09,143
but you've raised your three children...

334
00:17:09,213 --> 00:17:10,573
to be very respectable.

335
00:17:11,543 --> 00:17:12,983
Oh, hardly.

336
00:17:13,683 --> 00:17:15,713
They didn't all turn out exactly as I'd hoped,

337
00:17:16,253 --> 00:17:18,413
but I'm satisfied that they're diligent...

338
00:17:18,483 --> 00:17:19,953
and pull their own weight.

339
00:17:20,323 --> 00:17:22,183
That's what's most important, of course.

340
00:17:23,393 --> 00:17:26,123
- Your name is Bit Na? - Yes, Jo Bit Na.

341
00:17:26,423 --> 00:17:29,333
- I missed you, Great-Grandma. - Oh, my.

342
00:17:29,393 --> 00:17:32,633
- You too, Great-Grandpa. - Oh, really?

343
00:17:33,433 --> 00:17:36,003
This grandpa missed my great-granddaughter...

344
00:17:36,073 --> 00:17:37,073
very much too.

345
00:17:37,573 --> 00:17:40,203
You're so pretty and smart too.

346
00:17:41,473 --> 00:17:43,513
I heard you have a doctorate in philosophy,

347
00:17:43,813 --> 00:17:47,013
but because of the times, you can't land a teaching position?

348
00:17:47,013 --> 00:17:48,043
That's right.

349
00:17:48,483 --> 00:17:50,483
But, even if it's not at a university,

350
00:17:50,613 --> 00:17:53,353
I'm still able to fulfill my duty of teaching students,

351
00:17:53,583 --> 00:17:56,853
- so I don't have major complaints. - That's the spirit.

352
00:17:57,353 --> 00:18:00,263
Do you know how your mother and I first met?

353
00:18:01,393 --> 00:18:02,833
Our youngest granddaughter...

354
00:18:03,633 --> 00:18:07,963
- brought mother and me together. - What? I did?

355
00:18:08,833 --> 00:18:10,833
That's right. The day I first found out...

356
00:18:10,903 --> 00:18:12,233
you dropped out of school,

357
00:18:12,743 --> 00:18:14,743
I happened to run into your grandmother...

358
00:18:14,803 --> 00:18:16,113
in front of the hospital.

359
00:18:17,843 --> 00:18:18,973
Oh, I see.

360
00:18:19,683 --> 00:18:21,283
I'm back.

361
00:18:24,483 --> 00:18:25,483
Kang Yeon Ja.

362
00:18:26,053 --> 00:18:29,353
Well, look at this. The whole family's here.

363
00:18:29,923 --> 00:18:33,323
Come on, say hello. This is your great-aunt.

364
00:18:35,093 --> 00:18:36,333
- Hello. - Hello.

365
00:18:36,393 --> 00:18:39,263
Oh, yes, nice to meet you. Welcome.

366
00:18:39,333 --> 00:18:41,033
Yes, everyone, have a seat.

367
00:18:42,533 --> 00:18:44,203
What? It's that lady from before.

368
00:18:44,503 --> 00:18:47,873
- Grandma's friend who came over. - What?

369
00:18:48,673 --> 00:18:50,273
Have you seen me before?

370
00:18:50,343 --> 00:18:54,013
Yes. You came to our house and asked to see Grandma's necklace.

371
00:18:54,183 --> 00:18:56,153
You were so surprised when you saw it.

372
00:18:56,413 --> 00:18:58,983
What? I did? When?

373
00:18:59,053 --> 00:19:00,923
- Oh, for goodness' sake. - What is she talking about?

374
00:19:01,383 --> 00:19:02,593
A necklace?

375
00:19:03,453 --> 00:19:04,623
Don't tell me...

376
00:19:05,023 --> 00:19:06,123
When was this?

377
00:19:06,393 --> 00:19:08,863
No, it's just...

378
00:19:09,363 --> 00:19:11,563
It was a long time ago. It was nothing.

379
00:19:16,203 --> 00:19:19,103
My, what a sharp eye you have for a little kid.

380
00:19:20,173 --> 00:19:22,403
Excuse me. Father,

381
00:19:22,543 --> 00:19:25,213
I bought this outfit for the living funeral.

382
00:19:25,273 --> 00:19:28,883
- Would you like to see it? - No. I'll look at it later.

383
00:19:29,213 --> 00:19:31,483
Okay. I made sure it is very luxurious,

384
00:19:31,553 --> 00:19:33,083
befitting of a party,

385
00:19:33,153 --> 00:19:34,983
and I prepared something glamorous, Father.

386
00:19:37,153 --> 00:19:40,423
What? You mean all the grandkids and even the great-granddaughter?

387
00:19:41,893 --> 00:19:44,033
It seems she's really going all out.

388
00:19:45,533 --> 00:19:47,063
All right, I get it. I'll be home early.

389
00:19:47,863 --> 00:19:49,063
Yes. Okay, bye.

390
00:19:53,773 --> 00:19:54,843
Yes, come in.

391
00:19:55,273 --> 00:19:57,273
(Gangsu Construction)

392
00:19:58,873 --> 00:19:59,913
What brings you here?

393
00:20:00,443 --> 00:20:02,483
It's about the preparations for Grandfather's funeral.

394
00:20:02,543 --> 00:20:04,953
Seung Ri and I drafted a tentative program.

395
00:20:05,183 --> 00:20:06,223
Please take a look.

396
00:20:06,753 --> 00:20:09,523
Not you too. Is everyone okay with a funeral...

397
00:20:09,593 --> 00:20:13,263
- for someone who is still alive? - You know it's Grandfather's wish.

398
00:20:13,523 --> 00:20:17,533
Also, I am going to propose to Seung Ri again soon.

399
00:20:17,763 --> 00:20:18,763
I am just letting you know.

400
00:20:19,233 --> 00:20:20,763
What is wrong with you, seriously?

401
00:20:20,833 --> 00:20:24,003
Are you trying to give your father a heart attack?

402
00:20:24,073 --> 00:20:25,073
Father.

403
00:20:25,803 --> 00:20:28,873
You married Mom because you truly loved her, right?

404
00:20:29,513 --> 00:20:30,573
Of course.

405
00:20:31,543 --> 00:20:32,543
Why do you ask?

406
00:20:32,613 --> 00:20:35,783
If Grandfather had been against your marriage back then,

407
00:20:36,383 --> 00:20:38,113
would you have just given up?

408
00:20:38,453 --> 00:20:39,953
What? Of course not.

409
00:20:40,483 --> 00:20:42,383
How could I have given up on your mother?

410
00:20:42,483 --> 00:20:43,693
See? My point exactly.

411
00:20:44,353 --> 00:20:46,393
You would not have given up,

412
00:20:46,463 --> 00:20:50,393
- so why are you forcing me to? - No, our situations are different.

413
00:20:50,863 --> 00:20:51,863
Okay, fine.

414
00:20:51,963 --> 00:20:55,263
Let us say I am willing to give up on marrying you off for connections.

415
00:20:55,633 --> 00:20:56,633
But...

416
00:20:57,033 --> 00:21:00,403
Seo Gwon Sik and I can never be in-laws. Understand?

417
00:21:00,473 --> 00:21:03,873
But, why? Why are you two on such bad terms?

418
00:21:03,943 --> 00:21:05,543
There is no reason. It just cannot happen.

419
00:21:05,613 --> 00:21:06,683
It is absolutely impossible.

420
00:21:07,743 --> 00:21:09,913
Fine. If that is how you are going to be,

421
00:21:10,453 --> 00:21:11,753
I do not need your permission.

422
00:21:12,483 --> 00:21:15,623
I am not giving up on Seung Ri, no matter what. Just so you know.

423
00:21:16,053 --> 00:21:17,993
Hey, you. Hey, Ko Min Ho.

424
00:21:18,493 --> 00:21:21,123
That brat. Hey, you, take this. I said take this with you.

425
00:21:21,723 --> 00:21:22,893
Gosh. Unbelievable.

426
00:21:23,833 --> 00:21:25,393
Since the cost of purchasing land is...

427
00:21:25,463 --> 00:21:27,303
the biggest portion of the project budget,

428
00:21:27,503 --> 00:21:30,203
we must thoroughly vet its commercial viability.

429
00:21:30,473 --> 00:21:32,173
Yes, once we have the candidate sites,

430
00:21:32,233 --> 00:21:34,343
I will conduct a thorough comparative analysis.

431
00:21:34,543 --> 00:21:36,173
I'll also start by compiling a list of locations...

432
00:21:36,243 --> 00:21:37,673
that fit our Retirement Community's concept.

433
00:21:38,613 --> 00:21:40,683
Then I will pull some more related materials...

434
00:21:40,743 --> 00:21:42,513
from the archives before I head home.

435
00:21:42,613 --> 00:21:44,453
- See you tomorrow. - Yes, thank you for your hard work.

436
00:21:44,513 --> 00:21:45,513
Okay.

437
00:21:47,983 --> 00:21:48,983
Oh, right.

438
00:21:49,223 --> 00:21:51,193
What happened at the police station?

439
00:21:51,723 --> 00:21:52,723
It's not easy.

440
00:21:53,063 --> 00:21:54,563
The accident was so long ago that they said...

441
00:21:54,623 --> 00:21:55,863
it couldn't be found in the system.

442
00:21:56,263 --> 00:21:57,763
Instead, they traced it to the police station...

443
00:21:57,833 --> 00:21:58,833
that had jurisdiction,

444
00:21:58,893 --> 00:22:00,833
so I filed a request for the accident records there.

445
00:22:01,063 --> 00:22:04,233
- Are they able to look it up there? - No.

446
00:22:04,573 --> 00:22:06,243
Well, they said they would look,

447
00:22:06,303 --> 00:22:08,543
but the records may have been disposed of.

448
00:22:09,543 --> 00:22:11,313
I guess I will just have to wait and see.

449
00:22:12,213 --> 00:22:13,483
That's really tough.

450
00:22:14,613 --> 00:22:16,513
So that's why you looked so down all day.

451
00:22:17,513 --> 00:22:20,323
Well, you went through a lot today. You're heading straight home, right?

452
00:22:20,423 --> 00:22:21,883
How about we grab a quick dinner,

453
00:22:21,983 --> 00:22:24,293
and then work on the video for Grandfather's event together?

454
00:22:24,353 --> 00:22:27,223
Sure. How about we eat, take a walk to clear our heads,

455
00:22:27,293 --> 00:22:29,533
- and then come back? - Yes, let's do that.

456
00:22:31,263 --> 00:22:32,763
Hey, shouldn't we head home?

457
00:22:34,133 --> 00:22:35,133
Yes, I guess so.

458
00:22:36,933 --> 00:22:39,133
Oh, by the way, about Team Leader Ko.

459
00:22:41,303 --> 00:22:45,143
Do you know anything about how he was adopted by President Ko?

460
00:22:45,613 --> 00:22:48,913
What? Why do you ask?

461
00:22:49,513 --> 00:22:51,213
President Ko already has his own son,

462
00:22:51,283 --> 00:22:52,883
so I'm curious why he'd go out of his way...

463
00:22:52,953 --> 00:22:53,953
to adopt Team Leader Ko.

464
00:22:55,323 --> 00:22:58,853
They say President Ko only agreed because the Chairman told him to.

465
00:23:00,123 --> 00:23:02,023
Was he the son of an acquaintance of the Chairman?

466
00:23:04,763 --> 00:23:08,003
The Chairman? I am not sure.

467
00:23:09,263 --> 00:23:12,233
I just heard they got him from an orphanage.

468
00:23:13,673 --> 00:23:15,943
And President Ko just accepted that?

469
00:23:18,143 --> 00:23:19,243
That's surprising.

470
00:23:21,043 --> 00:23:22,613
I don't really know.

471
00:23:22,613 --> 00:23:24,553
But, if that's what President Ko said...

472
00:23:25,253 --> 00:23:27,223
I guess that must be it.

473
00:23:29,693 --> 00:23:31,693
Yes, I guess so.

474
00:23:33,023 --> 00:23:34,023
Let's head out.

475
00:23:41,963 --> 00:23:44,473
Honey. Today, I bought outfits for your parents...

476
00:23:44,533 --> 00:23:48,643
to wear at Father's living funeral, and for us too. Want to see?

477
00:23:51,043 --> 00:23:54,213
They said the theme is a fun and exciting party,

478
00:23:54,283 --> 00:23:56,583
so I picked out the most fabulous outfits for us.

479
00:23:57,653 --> 00:23:59,723
Crystal, are you being serious right now?

480
00:24:00,183 --> 00:24:01,953
What, am I the only one who thinks this is weird?

481
00:24:02,183 --> 00:24:04,653
Am I the only one who can't accept this funeral?

482
00:24:04,723 --> 00:24:08,123
Oh, please. Father's word is law.

483
00:24:08,193 --> 00:24:09,693
We have to do as he says. What other choice is there?

484
00:24:10,263 --> 00:24:13,133
No, I can't do it. Absolutely not.

485
00:24:14,733 --> 00:24:17,873
Oh, please. What are you going to do if you don't?

486
00:24:18,533 --> 00:24:22,143
What do you mean you're against it? I've explained everything,

487
00:24:22,203 --> 00:24:24,643
so why can't you understand what I want?

488
00:24:25,373 --> 00:24:29,143
I know. But, no matter how hard I try to understand and accept it...

489
00:24:30,083 --> 00:24:32,683
- I just can't do it. - Unbelievable.

490
00:24:33,353 --> 00:24:36,323
If you still have enough energy to hold your own funeral in advance,

491
00:24:37,053 --> 00:24:40,623
why won't you consider getting more aggressive treatment?

492
00:24:41,223 --> 00:24:44,263
Why are you trying to give up on your life already?

493
00:24:44,833 --> 00:24:47,763
Why are you being so stubborn? Why?

494
00:24:48,833 --> 00:24:53,443
It's because while I still have some energy left,

495
00:24:54,843 --> 00:24:59,913
I want to say a happy goodbye to the people I love.

496
00:25:01,013 --> 00:25:03,213
I'm not giving up on my life.

497
00:25:03,583 --> 00:25:07,523
I just want to wrap things up comfortably and naturally...

498
00:25:08,153 --> 00:25:11,653
- on my own terms. - That is giving up.

499
00:25:12,323 --> 00:25:15,123
It means you've lost your will to live, doesn't it?

500
00:25:16,563 --> 00:25:18,933
I know I may have been a disappointment as a son,

501
00:25:20,433 --> 00:25:22,973
but I really don't want you to die, Father.

502
00:25:23,873 --> 00:25:26,603
I know I've only disappointed you so far,

503
00:25:28,343 --> 00:25:29,403
and I know it's late,

504
00:25:29,913 --> 00:25:32,073
but from now on, I want to get my act together...

505
00:25:32,143 --> 00:25:33,713
and show you I can be a good son.

506
00:25:34,483 --> 00:25:36,283
I really want to show you that,

507
00:25:36,783 --> 00:25:39,383
so why are you only thinking about leaving?

508
00:25:40,223 --> 00:25:41,223
Ko Dae Chi.

509
00:25:42,423 --> 00:25:45,893
That sentiment is more than enough for me.

510
00:25:48,523 --> 00:25:49,833
Just as you've said,

511
00:25:50,463 --> 00:25:52,563
you just have to live like that from now on.

512
00:25:54,103 --> 00:25:56,163
Don't be greedy.

513
00:25:56,533 --> 00:25:59,403
Just live with a generous heart.

514
00:26:01,073 --> 00:26:02,343
If you do that,

515
00:26:03,543 --> 00:26:05,443
then I will have nothing more to ask of you.

516
00:26:06,983 --> 00:26:08,383
Father.

517
00:26:09,313 --> 00:26:10,453
Seriously.

518
00:26:12,453 --> 00:26:13,883
(Our Happy Days Real Estate, Grandma Pancake)

519
00:26:13,953 --> 00:26:15,023
I've been thinking.

520
00:26:15,083 --> 00:26:18,393
Even if the police station doesn't have the files anymore,

521
00:26:18,693 --> 00:26:20,963
the fact that the precinct is running a search...

522
00:26:21,023 --> 00:26:22,923
means a record of the case must exist.

523
00:26:23,433 --> 00:26:26,733
Then at least some basic information about the accident should be left.

524
00:26:27,963 --> 00:26:29,403
Based on that, there must be another way...

525
00:26:29,463 --> 00:26:30,573
to find what we're looking for.

526
00:26:31,433 --> 00:26:32,873
For now, we just have to wait.

527
00:26:33,603 --> 00:26:37,543
Also, what about asking your grandfather?

528
00:26:38,343 --> 00:26:42,183
You said your father was a valued employee of his, right?

529
00:26:42,543 --> 00:26:44,153
Don't you think he might know something?

530
00:26:44,213 --> 00:26:46,723
He might, but he's not well.

531
00:26:47,223 --> 00:26:49,793
If he finds out I'm doing this, he'll just worry more,

532
00:26:50,053 --> 00:26:51,723
so I was trying not to tell him if possible.

533
00:26:52,293 --> 00:26:53,863
Don't worry too much.

534
00:26:54,293 --> 00:26:56,833
I'm sure we'll find an answer if we keep looking.

535
00:26:57,663 --> 00:26:59,333
- We should go in. - Okay.

536
00:27:06,943 --> 00:27:08,243
Still not home yet?

537
00:27:08,703 --> 00:27:10,573
I was hoping to talk about the site selection.

538
00:27:23,293 --> 00:27:24,293
Father.

539
00:27:26,923 --> 00:27:28,693
Hey, Team Leader Ko.

540
00:27:57,593 --> 00:28:00,423
(Our Happy Days)

541
00:28:01,463 --> 00:28:03,463
Oh, dear. What's wrong?

542
00:28:03,593 --> 00:28:04,763
Oh my, are you all right?

543
00:28:04,763 --> 00:28:06,533
We can still cancel. Okay?

544
00:28:06,603 --> 00:28:08,403
There won't be a next time.

545
00:28:08,563 --> 00:28:10,603
The Cheongbin Police Traffic Investigation Unit?

546
00:28:10,673 --> 00:28:11,673
Have you found anything?

547
00:28:11,733 --> 00:28:13,403
You need to get that look off your face.

548
00:28:13,773 --> 00:28:15,973
People will think something is wrong.

549
00:28:16,173 --> 00:28:17,273
I have brought you all here today...

550
00:28:17,343 --> 00:28:22,483
to share a joyful and happy farewell.

551
00:28:22,583 --> 00:28:25,853
Thank you for being a part of my life.

552
00:28:31,523 --> 00:28:34,523
(Our Happy Days)
